[size=5]Apocalypse — Magic of Skyrim — Enderal Patch[/size]

[i]Enai Siaion's Apocalypse, made to actually work in Enderal: Forgotten Stories — and to stop sounding like Tamriel.[/i]

Apocalypse adds 373 spells. In Enderal, out of the box, you can obtain [b]none of them[/b]. Not one vendor stocks a tome, not one chest drops a scroll, and not one staff can be crafted. The spells are all there, mechanically fine, sitting in a plugin that has no way to hand them to you.

This patch gives them a way in, retires the parts that cannot work here, and takes the Daedra out of a world that has never heard of them.

[line]

[size=4]⚠ Requirements — read this part[/size]

[list]
[*][b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/1090]Apocalypse — Magic of Skyrim by Enai Siaion[/url][/b], version [b]10.2.3[/b]. Install it normally.
[*][b]Keep [font=Courier New]Apocalypse - Magic of Skyrim.esp[/font] ENABLED[/b] and load this patch [b]after[/b] it. This is a patch, not a replacement — all the spells, meshes and textures come from Enai's mod.
[/list]

[b]That is the whole list — there is nothing to tick.[/b] Apocalypse declares [font=Courier New]Dragonborn.esm[/font] as a master, which normally sounds alarming in Enderal. It isn't: Enderal ships a 44 KB stub of that file and the SSE engine force-loads it along with the other two DLC stubs whether or not they appear in your plugin list. Confirmed by reading the plugin table out of a running game — [font=Courier New]Dragonborn.esm[/font] sits at index 3 in a profile that never enabled it. This patch still clears the references that pointed into it, so nothing meaningful is left dangling.

[line]

[size=4]Why Apocalypse does nothing in Enderal[/size]

Not an exaggeration, and not a balance complaint. Two independent failures:

[list=1]
[*][b]Its entire distribution system targets records Enderal does not have.[/b] Apocalypse runs a quest at game start that copies its tomes, scrolls and staves into [b]54 vanilla Skyrim vendor and loot leveled lists[/b]. Enderal replaced [font=Courier New]Skyrim.esm[/font] wholesale — it is base Enderal, not Bethesda's game — and [b]not one of those 54 lists exists[/b]. Neither do the five College of Winterhold ritual globals the mod gates part of its distribution on, nor the [font=Courier New]Tamriel[/font] worldspace it places its utility containers in. The quest runs, copies nothing into nothing, and reports success.
[*][b]Its staff crafting is built on Dragonborn content.[/b] All 67 staff recipes are made at the [b]Staff Enchanter[/b] out of [b]Heart Stones[/b]. Enderal has neither.
[*][b]It overwrites one of Enderal's worldspaces.[/b] Apocalypse edits worldspace [font=Courier New]00003C[/font], which in Skyrim is [b]Tamriel[/b] — but in Enderal that ID belongs to [b]MQP01Home[/b], the prologue house. Its edit stamps Tamriel's map grid over it, drops the parent link to Vyn and the no-fast-travel flags, and attaches a region list of five IDs of which four do not exist in Enderal and the fifth is a stone wall.
[/list]

Enderal also has no spell tomes at all — it teaches spells from its own spellbooks, fed by its own leveled lists. So there was nowhere for Apocalypse's tomes to land even in principle until something put them there.

[line]

[size=4]What this patch does[/size]

[b]1. Distribution — the part that makes the mod exist.[/b]

[b]160 spell tomes[/b] and [b]130 scrolls[/b] are added to Enderal's own vendor and loot lists, tiered by spell rank so a novice does not find a master spell at level 3:

[code]
  Apocalypse rank      Enderal tier              Roughly
  Novice   (000)       Trader/Loot A             level 1+
  Apprentice (025)     Trader/Loot A and B       level 5-10+
  Adept    (050)       Trader/Loot C             level 18+
  Expert   (075)       Trader/Loot C and D       level 30+
  Master   (100)       Trader/Loot D             level 40+
[/code]

Scrolls go into Enderal's general scroll loot pool. Buy tomes from mages and traders, find them in the world, exactly as you find Enderal's own.

This is done by [b]adding[/b] a single entry to each of Enderal's nine lists, pointing at this patch's own sublists. Every entry Enderal already had is carried through untouched — nothing of the base game's loot is displaced or replaced.

[b]2. Staff crafting stays dead, and the patch leaves it alone.[/b]

All 67 recipes are built at the [b]Staff Enchanter[/b] out of [b]Heart Stones[/b], and Enderal has neither — so every one of them is already unreachable in Apocalypse's own records, before this patch does anything. Both the bench keyword and the component point at Dragonborn FormIDs that resolve to nothing here, which means the recipes belong to no crafting menu and can never be listed. The staves are not distributed either.

Earlier builds of this patch overrode all 67 records to null their bench keyword. That has been dropped: it changed nothing a player could observe, and no recipe anywhere in Enderal's 1,859 has a null bench keyword, so it was inventing a record shape the game never uses. Enderal's own enchanter is untouched.

[b]3. Fabricate Object drops its Staff Enchanter option.[/b]

The spell that conjures a temporary crafting station offered nine, one of them the Dragonborn Staff Enchanter. It now offers the [b]eight[/b] that exist in Enderal — Arcane Enchanter, Alchemy Lab, Tanning Rack, Workbench, Anvil, Cooking Spit, Grindstone, Smelter — all of them present and working. The menu and the station list are index-matched, so both were trimmed together; picking "Smelter" still gives you a smelter.

[b]3b. The prologue house is put back.[/b]

Apocalypse's edit to worldspace [font=Courier New]00003C[/font] is reverted to Enderal's own [font=Courier New]MQP01Home[/font] record, forwarded from Forgotten Stories so nothing FS changed is lost. That restores its parent link to Vyn, its map offsets, its [i]small world[/i] and [i]no fast travel[/i] flags, and removes the region list pointing at forms Enderal does not have.

[b]4. Fifteen summons removed.[/b]

Enderal has no Daedra and no Dwemer. These are never added to any vendor or loot list:

[list]
[*][b]Dremora[/b] — Churl, Pit Fighter, Champion, Honor Guard, Mentor, Assassin
[*][b]Xivilai[/b] — Sorcerer, Lord
[*][b]Other Daedra[/b] — Weeping Daedra, Lord of Bindings, Six Demon Bag, Conjure Herne, Conjure Kyrkrim
[*][b]Atronach Mark[/b] — summons atronachs onto the marked target
[*][b]Conjure Craftlord[/b] — a Dwemer automaton
[/list]

Everything else in Apocalypse's conjuration school stays: the wraiths, liches, totem spirits, the Battlemage, the Necrowitch, the Deadeye Captain, Bag of Rats. Enderal's own magic already raises the dead and binds spirits — [i]Entropy[/i] is one of its five disciplines — so undead and spirit summoning is entirely at home here. Only the Oblivion natives had to go.

[b]5. Elder Scrolls names replaced.[/b]

See the table below.

[line]

[size=4]The renamed spells[/size]

Every replacement is drawn from Enderal's own written lore — its seven gods, its named scholars, its geography — not invented. Renames are applied to every place the name appears: the tome, the spell, the scroll, the magic effect, the enchantment and the description text.

[b]Gods, the world, and the planes[/b]

