[line]

[size=4]What is NOT changed[/size]

[list]
[*][b]No spell balance changes.[/b] Damage, cost, duration and cooldowns are Enai's. Enderal keeps all five of Skyrim's magic skills and only renames them, so Apocalypse's spells scale off your Elementalism, Entropy, Light Magic, Mentalism and Psionics without any conversion at all.
[*][b]No new spells, no removed records.[/b] The fifteen cut summons are still in Apocalypse; they are simply never handed to you.
[*][b]No Enderal records rewritten.[/b] The nine leveled lists are appended to, never edited.
[/list]

For reference, in case you have wondered which Enderal skill governs an Apocalypse spell:

[code]
  Skyrim school     Enderal discipline    Higher school
  Destruction       Elementalism          (its own art)
  Conjuration       Entropy               Sinistra
  Restoration       Light Magic           Thaumaturgy
  Alteration        Mentalism             Thaumaturgy
  Illusion          Psionics              Sinistra
[/code]

Note the last two — Alteration is [i]Mentalism[/i] and Illusion is [i]Psionics[/i], not the pairing you would guess.

[line]

[size=4]Compatibility and load order[/size]

The plugin is [b]ESL-flagged[/b], so it costs nothing against the 254-plugin limit.

Load it [b]after[/b] [font=Courier New]Apocalypse - Magic of Skyrim.esp[/font]. It overrides records from Apocalypse and appends to nine of Enderal's leveled lists:

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]_00ETraderSpellBooksLevelA[/font] through [font=Courier New]D[/font] — the spellbook vendor tiers
[*][font=Courier New]_00E_SpellBooksLootA[/font] through [font=Courier New]D[/font] — the spellbook loot tiers
[*][font=Courier New]00E_ScrollsLowChance[/font] — the scroll loot pool
[/list]

If another mod also edits those nine lists, the later plugin wins outright and one mod's additions are lost — either load order accordingly or merge them with a Bashed/Smashed patch, as with any leveled list conflict.

[b]Pinned to Apocalypse 10.2.3.[/b] This patch overrides specific records by ID. If Enai releases a version that moves things, the patch needs refreshing — do not assume a newer Apocalypse is safe with it.

[line]

[size=4]Known limitations[/size]

[list]
[*][b]The 67 staves are unobtainable.[/b] Deliberate — see above. If you want them, the console still works.
[*][b]Banish Living has no visual effect[/b], and a couple of spells that would have spoken a line stay silent. Both are Apocalypse pointing at vanilla Skyrim records Enderal does not have. They are cosmetic, and inventing replacements would have meant guessing at Enai's intent, so they were left alone and written down instead.
[*][b]Scroll inventory previews and one summoned sword's first-person model are missing[/b] — Apocalypse points all 144 scrolls at a vanilla display model Enderal lacks. The patch forwards that reference unchanged rather than stripping it from the handful of scrolls it touches, so all 144 behave identically instead of ten being quietly different.
[*][b]Spell tome tiering is by rank name, not by playtested power.[/b] A master-rank Apocalypse spell arrives around level 40 because it is master-rank, not because it was measured against Enderal's difficulty curve. Feedback welcome.
[*][b]Requires Enderal SE[/b], which is pinned to Skyrim SE [b]1.5.97[/b]. This is a plugin only, so no SKSE version concerns apply to it.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4]Credits[/size]

[b]Enai Siaion[/b] — Apocalypse, all 373 spells, and every asset involved. This patch contains no assets and no spells of its own; it is plumbing so that his work reaches you in a different game. Go endorse [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/1090]the original[/url].
[b]SureAI[/b] — Enderal: Forgotten Stories, and the written lore every replacement name was taken from.

Built from Spriggit YAML sources. Every record was checked against Enderal's own serialized plugins rather than assumed from Skyrim modding habits — which is how the dead distribution was found in the first place.
